  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Soulive 3-8-11 d1t07** (1 other source): Whatcha See Is Whatcha Get featured guest John Scofield [1]\n- The reviewer identifies the performance referred to as the \"blues song\" as Today I Sing the Blues [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Soulive 3-8-11 d1t01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Soulive 3-8-11 d1t02**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Soulive 3-8-11 d1t03**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Soulive 3-8-11 d1t04**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Soulive 3-8-11 d1t05**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Soulive 3-8-11 d1t06**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Soulive 3-8-11 d1t07**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Soulive 3-8-11 d1t08**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **Soulive2011-03-08** (recommended): source not stated; 19 songs; 120 min [1]\n- **soulive2011-03-08.flac16.140s**: source not stated; 19 songs; 120 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Set 2 included guests Ivan Neville and John Scofield; the Shady Horns joined: Igmar Thomas on trumpet, James Casey and Ryan Zoidis on saxophones [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **Soulive2011-03-08**: Recorded with Neumann SKM 140 microphones feeding an Edirol R44 recorder [1]\n- **soulive2011-03-08.flac16.140s**: taped by Frank D'Auria; transferred by Frank D'Auria; source: Neumann SKM 140 ->Edirol R44 [2]",
